From: FF7 local performance investigation
Subject: [EXPERIMENT E07] drm/amdgpu: batch exact replacements across stable VRAM BOs

Apply after E01/E03/E04 to pinned CachyOS 7.2.8-1. Default mode remains the
E04 narrow behavior. Runtime ff7_vm_cross_bo=1 extends only operation 0xf704
when old and new VRAM BOs share the locked VM reservation, both are stable,
and the old mapping is exactly the requested 64 KiB with an existing leaf.
PRT and non-exact ranges still fall back before mutation. No changed UAPI,
IB size, batch bound, implicit dependencies, TLB retirement or GPU waits.
Read the mode once per operation; ordinary applications do not opt in.
Hardware correctness/performance require the supplied new two-BO gate.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_gem.c
@@ -844,7 +844,72 @@
